WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.817
This slide gives the four main row-preservation
patterns INNER JOIN keeps

00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:10.267
only row combinations where the match condition is
true If a patient

00:00:10.293 --> 00:00:14.530
has no admission that patient is absent from a
patient-to-admission INNER JOIN

00:00:16.287 --> 00:00:20.763
LEFT JOIN keeps every row from the left table When
no right-side

00:00:20.776 --> 00:00:26.532
match exists right-side columns become NULL RIGHT
JOIN is the mirror

00:00:26.558 --> 00:00:31.561
image Every row from the right table is preserved
and unmatched left-side

00:00:31.587 --> 00:00:37.195
columns become NULL FULL OUTER JOIN preserves
unmatched rows from both

00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:42.171
sides This is especially useful when reconciling a
master table with an

00:00:42.184 --> 00:00:48.735
external staging source Do not memorize these as
shapes only Read

00:00:48.761 --> 00:00:54.261
them as population rules Ask what population must
remain complete

00:00:55.169 --> 00:00:58.788
If the answer is all patients put patients on the
preserved side

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:02.998
That simple question often makes the join choice
much easier
